WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.068
-I'm a little embarrassed
by this,

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.336
because
I think there are probably

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.704
a lot of people watching at home
who would say, like,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.006
"You know,
you're not actually nailing it."

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.508
And, for the record,
I forgot to record our sound.

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:12.278
So it will get --
my audio will get better

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.780
about halfway through
this interview.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.750
But are you proud
of how you've learned

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.687
to technically execute
your podcast,

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.222
considering that,
I'm assuming, like me,

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:25.057
you did not have
any of this training?

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:26.492
-No, 100%.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:29.395
It was a major learning curve

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.297
getting
all the technology right,

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.566
like, having to have
the headphones into the computer

00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:36.336
so I could hear
the other actors,

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:41.140
but one off, because
we didn't want it bleeding over,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.009
forgetting to push "stop"
on record.

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.478
You know, definitely.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.080
But that --
I mean, just the fact

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.117
that I actually had something
that I could work on

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.587
during the quarantine was...
-Yeah.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.056
-...talk about, like,
a bonus gift.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:00.092
This was something that was
set up at the end of last year,

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:02.361
so I was already planning
to do it.

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.530
I just didn't know
that I would be doing it

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.233
from my bathroom in Idaho.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.701
-No. It is true.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.570
I mean, it is such
a good fortune that you had.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.140
And this is a podcast that
you're producing, as well.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.176
And this -- we should say
this is "Dirty Diana."

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.444
It's available now.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:21.614
And it is --
there is some mature content.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.416
-Yes. There is.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.750
-And you --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.620
And, now,
I will say that even --

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.888
like, I feel like

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.991
one of the first things
I was aware of, of you,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:35.361
is that you have
this really iconic voice.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.364
Like, is it fun
to use it in a way like this

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.765
that I'm assuming you --

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:42.201
have you ever done just straight
voice work like this before?

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.036
-I mean,
I've done some voice-overs,

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:46.573
but nothing like, you know --

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:49.308
what I remember
hearing people talk about.

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:50.977
"Oh, yeah, you know,
in the old days,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.278
when they had the radio shows

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.214
and everyone
would gather around."

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.949
And...

00:01:56.949 --> 00:02:01.020
And it was definitely
a really cool experience --

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.855
I mean, literally,
just like this,

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:06.292
acting out scenes with actors.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.928
And I -- my -- you know,

00:02:09.928 --> 00:02:11.664
I guess
I don't think of my voice

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.500
'cause like most people...
-Of course.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.670
-...I can't stand
hearing myself speak.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.473
But I'm glad that
whatever others see about it

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:23.909
works for this.

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:27.279
-This is --
Basically, you are --

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:28.848
not to give too much away
of the plot,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:32.551
but you help women
record erotica.

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:35.054
Is that like a pretty decent
description of it?

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.089
-Yeah. So at the heart of it --
-It's very steamy.

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:38.691
I've listened --
I listened to an episode.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.892
It's very steamy.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.561
-I noticed that you just sat
back there, Seth,

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.562
a little like --
like a little closing off.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:47.266
-I will say
I found it very titillating

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.734
and then a little bit less so

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:52.137
when I realized you filmed it
in a carpeted bathroom.

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:53.505
[ Laughs ]
-That takes --

00:02:53.505 --> 00:02:55.508
Does that
take the sexiness away?

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.009
-It was a little bit --

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.779
When I pictured you on a tiny
couch in a carpeted bathroom,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.214
it was a little bit less sexy,

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:04.016
but I'm sure for someone out
there, that made it more sexy.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:08.654
-Well, the good news is it's
just all about our imaginations.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:11.090
So you can change that picture.
[ Dog barking ]

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.792
And -- Sorry. Sorry.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:16.529
Did somebody just get their eyes
on a giant tennis ball?

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:19.132
-Murple. Murps, no.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.267
-This was -- That was --
I do want to clarify,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.068
'cause we talked a little bit
ahead of time.

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:24.837
I feel like people
might watch and wonder

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.405
why you just said "Murps."

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:27.540
-Murps, yes.
-Your dog's name is Murple.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.108
Yeah.
-They're all --

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.077
and the rest are all going crazy
in the other room.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.113
I am hoping that's
not bleeding over into our...

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.315
-No. I -- Murple's
the first one we've heard, so...

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.817
-Okay.
-I mean, again,

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.186
I want to keep going back
to giving you credit

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.821
for figuring
how to record a podcast.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.122
-Oh, yeah.
-I feel like

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.556
not a lot of people
have seven dogs in the house

00:03:44.556 --> 00:03:48.094
when they're trying to record
a very erotic podcast.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.229
[ Laughs ]
-Yep. It was quite amazing.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:54.466
Imagine, like, having to do
these scenes, which --

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:56.035
not just the erotica part,

00:03:56.035 --> 00:04:01.908
which is really trying
to open up the window of --

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:05.644
from the female gaze
and really, you know,

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:10.416
take you down into the stories
that, in particular,

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:15.121
are reflective
of a woman's fantasy.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:18.424
We certainly know plenty
about men's.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.892
And...
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.494
But this also is dealing

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.963
with a relationship
that's very fractured.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.232
And, you know,
at the heart of this,

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:30.636
it's about a relationship
really being at its bottom

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:32.938
and making its way back.

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:35.842
But I'm sitting in
my little, tiny bathroom

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.244
with carpet...
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:43.016
-...and the giant
Joan of Arc statue

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:46.785
that's excellent for holding
the towels after they're wet.

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:48.554
-[ Laughs ]
-And then --

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.956
-That's -- What a -- What a --

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:53.859
What a great tribute
to Joan's sacrifice.

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:55.394
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:58.564
-She's looking out for me, Seth.
She's looking out for me.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.732
-There you go.
-But I would have these scenes

00:05:00.732 --> 00:05:03.669
where I'm -- we did where
it's in a therapist's office,

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:05.671
and we're, like,
screaming at each other.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.206
And then we'd go
on our lunch break,

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.876
and I'd go out into the kitchen,
and there's everybody.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.077
"Hey!"
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:14.647
So that's pretty cool.
-Well, it certainly --

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.249
the result -- it was worth
the hard work you put into it.

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:21.154
You also, again, I feel like
people must've been happy

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:23.122
to have finished
filming something

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.690
that can then be released now,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.626
because, obviously,
so much work has been stopped.

00:05:27.626 --> 00:05:30.363
So you have a show,
"Brave New World,"

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:32.331
on Peacock...
-I think it's --

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:33.499
-...coming out on Peacock.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:37.870
-Yes. And it airs on the 15th,
I think?

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.171
I could be wrong.
-Yeah, tomorrow.

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:43.409
-But the 15th, and --
Which is really exciting --

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.344
I'm, you know,
a small piece of it.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:48.147
I just did a little bit of it.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.849
But I really think the show

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:55.922
is going to really capture
people's attention.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:58.324
It's a -- you know,
it's an amazing book.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:02.561
And to see it translated
into something

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:04.830
that I think
will be great entertainment

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:08.734
and certainly needed
new content for now.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.268
-I could not agree
with you more.

00:06:10.268 --> 00:06:11.537
I'm so excited to see it.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.340
And it has just been delightful
talking to you.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.043
Thank you so much for making
the time for us today.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:21.280
-Thank you, Seth. Enjoy your,
uh, fireplace of stone.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.349
-[ Laughing ] Yes.
Let us -- We'll both --

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:26.918
-I like your --
I like your man behind you, too,

00:06:26.918 --> 00:06:28.921
your -- your -- your --
-Yes. We got a sea captain.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:32.090
I'm very lucky that, you know,
again, you have to find --

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.159
you know, you try to find
interesting backgrounds

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:35.227
for these things.

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:36.763
And I'm very lucky that
my in-laws

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:40.866
are collectors of sea captains
and ships, tiny ships, so...

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:42.868
-Oh, I have a feeling that

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.437
I would get along really well
with your in-laws.

00:06:45.437 --> 00:06:48.607
-Yeah, I think so, too,
especially, yeah, again,

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:52.144
that's far smaller
than a normal boat would be.

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:53.346
-Yep.
-Just like your couch.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:55.647
-Exactly.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:55.647 --> 00:06:56.849
We'll see you next time,
hopefully in person.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:57.917
-Okay.

